 ;; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ;; KNOWN FALSE-POSITIVE CLASS (PA3z, 2026-09-06). The mirror of PA2z's
 ;; false-negative finding, and it should be held with the same seriousness: an
 ;; instrument that OVER-reports in prose is no more trustworthy than one that
 ;; UNDER-reports in call arguments.
 ;;
 ;; Both pattern versions match inside DOCSTRINGS AND COMMENTS. Measured case:
 ;; node_sim.clj:165 is `{:node :R5` occurring inside the docstring of
 ;; `carriers!`, where it illustrates the shape of a carriers declaration. It is
 ;; prose. It is not code, and it links nothing.
 ;;
 ;; NOT FIXED BY WIDENING OR NARROWING THE REGEX -- a regex cannot see the
 ;; difference between a form and a docstring that contains one. The honest
 ;; handling is the one this ledger already uses everywhere else: the mechanical
 ;; layer reports a HIT, and a reading disposes of it. Recorded here so a future
 ;; slice does not credit a cell from a docstring, and so the count of what the
 ;; instrument cannot decide by itself stays visible rather than implied.
 :known-false-positive-class
 {:class :match-inside-docstring-or-comment
  :measured-case "futon2/src/futon2/aif/node_sim.clj:165 -- {:node :R5 inside the carriers! docstring"
  :affects [:v1 :v2]
  :disposition "Reported as a hit; disposed of by reading, never auto-credited. See PA3z's slice artifact for the R5 adjudication."}

